csp-panel (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Resellers: the panel now has users of its own. A reseller logs in with
    his own password, sees only his own clients and sells out of a credit
    balance (1 credit = 1 month of one line). Creating charges the months
    asked for, renewing extends from the later of today and the current
    expiry, deleting refunds nothing. Administrators see everything and pay
    nothing. State lives in /var/lib/csp-panel/resellers.json: scrypt
    passwords, balances, ownership, expiry and a ledger of every movement.
  * Accounts: expiry column with days left, a renew action, and the panel
    tracks expiry itself so it also works on backends without such a field.
  * New Resellers tab (admin): create, top up, enable, disable, delete and
    the credit history.
  * Visual overhaul: layered dark palette, translucent top bar, pill
    navigation, stat cards with tabular figures and state colours, sticky
    table headers, accessible focus rings and a usable mobile layout.
  * install-ubuntu.sh: --add-reseller, --serve-clients (NCam attends your
    clients over newcamd and cccam, no proxy needed), --remove-csp,
    --status, --credentials, --reset-password, --add-user, --add-reader,
    --migrate-users, --only-ncam and --all.
  * Fixed: the proxy.xml the installer writes needs ver="0.9.0", the
    CardServProxy unit must pass -Dcom.bowman.cardserv.allowanyjvm=true and
    the path of its config, and an account must be written inside
    <auth-config> to be seen by SimpleUserManager.

 -- CSP Panel contributors <noreply@example.com>  Sun, 05 Oct 2025 06:30:00 +0000

csp-panel (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Accounts tab: create, edit and delete the client accounts of a
    CardServProxy from the panel. They are the <user> elements of
    proxy.xml, edited in place (comments and formatting survive) and
    posted back through /cfgHandler.
  * New csp-cache-node daemon: a peer in the CSP cache cluster, speaking
    the same udp protocol as CardServProxy's ClusteredCache and NCam's
    csp_port. The panel reads its stats and shows them in a Cache tab:
    peers, round trip times, entries held and live entries.
  * install-ubuntu.sh --all installs the whole stack in one command:
    panel + NCam + CardServProxy + cache peer, wired together.
  * install-ubuntu.sh --install-csp builds the java proxy with plain
    javac (packaging/build-csp.sh) and configures both sides of the
    newcamd and cache links.
  * Fixed: saving a configuration file never worked against a real
    OSCam/NCam. Their webif looks for a literal "Content-Length: ", so
    the lower-case header fetch sends made every save time out.
  * Fixed: every config file was reported read-only, because the webif
    fills its writable flag before computing it.
  * Fixed: a softcam with no accounts yet (userstats answers "Invalid
    client") blanked out the whole dashboard.

 -- CSP Panel contributors <noreply@example.com>  Sun, 05 Oct 2025 04:00:00 +0000

csp-panel (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add the NCam backend (OSCam fork): /ncamapi.html endpoint, <ncam>
    document root and ncam.* configuration files, selected with
    BACKEND=ncam + NCAM_URL in /etc/csp-panel/panel.env.
  * The panel version is now read from the installed package.json, so
    /api/meta reports the real package version.
  * install-ubuntu.sh: --backend ncam, and the sources are fetched
    automatically when the script is run standalone.
  * panel.env documents the NCam settings and remote softcams.

 -- CSP Panel contributors <noreply@example.com>  Sat, 04 Oct 2025 12:00:00 +0000

csp-panel (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First Debian package of the modern CSP/OSCam panel: Node BFF plus
    React SPA under /usr/lib/csp-panel, hardened systemd unit running as
    the unprivileged csp-panel user, /etc/csp-panel/panel.env conffile.
  * Runtime dependencies are vendored, so installing needs no network.
  * One-shot installer for Ubuntu 20.04/22.04/24.04.

